From 88f304c89d68df61abbcf13943c72f9ecfddad4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:54:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp2: Add missing STM32MP255 cases to get_eth_nb()

get_eth_nb() enumerates every STM32MP25x CPU variant to decide how
many MAC addresses to expect in OTP, but the switch has no case for
any STM32MP255 part (255F/255D/255C/255A). On a board built around
one of those (e.g. CPU: STM32MP255FAK), get_cpu_type() falls through
to the default case and get_eth_nb() returns 0, so
setup_mac_address() returns immediately without ever touching OTP -
every MAC address stays unset regardless of what is actually fused.

STM32MP255 is the same silicon as STM32MP257 without the TSN switch,
so it has the same two GMACs as STM32MP253 and needs the same MAC
count.

Signed-off-by: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/stm32mp25x.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/stm32mp25x.c b/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/stm32mp25x.c
index 0d199f6f903..2ac8bdefbc3 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/stm32mp25x.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-stm32mp/stm32mp2/stm32mp25x.c
@@ -78,6 +78,14 @@ int get_eth_nb(void)
 	case CPU_STM32MP257Axx:
 		nb_eth = 5; /* dual ETH with TSN support */
 		break;
+	case CPU_STM32MP255Fxx:
+		fallthrough;
+	case CPU_STM32MP255Dxx:
+		fallthrough;
+	case CPU_STM32MP255Cxx:
+		fallthrough;
+	case CPU_STM32MP255Axx:
+		fallthrough;
 	case CPU_STM32MP253Fxx:
 		fallthrough;
 	case CPU_STM32MP253Dxx:
@@ -85,7 +93,7 @@ int get_eth_nb(void)
 	case CPU_STM32MP253Cxx:
 		fallthrough;
 	case CPU_STM32MP253Axx:
-		nb_eth = 2; /* dual ETH */
+		nb_eth = 2; /* dual ETH, no TSN switch */
 		break;
 	case CPU_STM32MP251Fxx:
 		fallthrough;
-- 
